This is the GreenREFORM-EU 2.0 **website** workspace. Write only here. Treat
the mounted `FinalVersion` and `Background material` roots as read-only.
When reading the documentation, prefer the compiled PDF of the current master
if it is present; otherwise use the live `_EN` files named in the master.

Task for now: information architecture and page copy in `content/`. Do not
build a visual design system or a live site unless asked.

British English. Short sentences. Public name is GreenREFORM-EU (hyphen).
This edition is GreenREFORM-EU 2.0. Call the technology sub-model the energy
technology model. Hard-linked, not soft-linked. Open source is allowed, but
name no licence (MIT or other) until DREAM confirms the text. No unused
household/monetary/public-optimisation features.

TSI 2026 is parked (10 November 2026): do not mention the project on the site,
by name or by implication, until the contract is settled. See
`content/parked/tsi-2026.md`. The paragraph below applies again on restoring.

The site will not launch before the Commission grant agreement is signed, so
TSI 2026 (ECONCLIMA2) may be described as a real project. Its conversion of
the code to Julia and its interface to external energy-system models are
project work, not properties of the documented 2.0 model, which is GAMS with
Python and gamY and is hard-linked.

57 industries belong to the Danish benchmark data, not to the model in the
abstract. Check live `\GREUchapter` lines in the highest-numbered master,
currently `greu_master_merged_v3_EN.tex`, before citing chapter files.
The published PDF is `content/Documentation/greu_master_merged_v4_EN.pdf`;
read it in preference to the `v3` PDF.

Prefer the foreword and Chapter 1 for homepage copy. Summarise chapters; do
not paste them. Point to the `.tex` section used. Follow `AGENTS.md` and
`WEBSITE_BRIEF.md`. Local KR/TSI narrative is in `Background material/` and
`content/background-notes.md`. Those files also hold staff names and candid
assessments of how each country team is doing: neither goes on the site.
